{
  "chapter": "evals/datasets",
  "tier": "build",
  "notes": [
    "Twenty cases is a smoke test. A release decision needs a set built on purpose, and one",
    "golden set per route rather than one for the application \u2014 a blended score hides a",
    "collapse in one route behind stability in the others.",
    "Four buckets: a stratified production sample, an adversarial library, constructed edge",
    "cases, and replays of failures that shipped. A set not growing from production failures",
    "has stopped learning.",
    "Harvest the centre, synthesise the edges. That is the opposite of the instinct, because",
    "synthetic data collapses to modal phrasing and skews formal where users are casual.",
    "Never generate eval data with the model family you are evaluating. A suspiciously high",
    "synthetic score is a suspicion about the set first.",
    "Two annotators on the same guidance should agree. Below the floor the labels are noise,",
    "and a disagreeing pair is a spec bug rather than an annotator problem.",
    "A set harvested from production is a second copy of customer data, with a different",
    "lifetime and usually worse discipline than the system it came from.",
    "The ceiling is judge cost rather than statistics, so past it stratified sampling beats",
    "growing the set. Agreement is in basis points so both tracks round identically."
  ],
  "policy": {
    "maxPerRoute": 6,
    "requiredBuckets": [
      "production",
      "adversarial",
      "constructed",
      "replay"
    ],
    "minKappaBps": 7000,
    "evaluatedFamily": "atlas-model",
    "productionFreshnessDays": 90,
    "rubricsPerCase": 4,
    "judgeCallBudget": 40
  },
  "cases": [
